# mikehoffmann.co — Entrepreneurship Collective
#
# Signups need exactly ONE of the three provider blocks below. Until one is
# set, the form returns a visible "not connected yet" error instead of a
# success screen it cannot honour. Set these in the Vercel project's
# Environment Variables, not in a committed file.

# ── Option 1: beehiiv ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# BEEHIIV_API_KEY=
# BEEHIIV_PUBLICATION_ID=pub_xxxxxxxx

# ── Option 2: Kit (formerly ConvertKit) ────────────────────────────────────
# KIT_API_KEY=
# KIT_FORM_ID=

# ── Option 3: anything else, via webhook (Zapier / Make / n8n / a CRM) ─────
# Receives { email, source, publication, submitted_at } as JSON.
# SUBSCRIBE_WEBHOOK_URL=

# Canonical origin. Only needed before the custom domain is attached — once
# mikehoffmann.co is on the project, Vercel supplies it automatically.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://mikehoffmann.co
